@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Contract
+
+Only wide direct-Arrow streams (at least 64 output columns), public row ceilings
+at least 64, no optional byte budget and supported primitive logical/physical
+builders may batch. Unsupported/narrow/small/byte-budget streams retain their
+complete existing path. Managed and explicit unmanaged projections share this
+eligibility; no predicate, key discovery, fetching or readiness rule changes.
+
+Decode all required fields in metadata order before output work. Retain existing
+fitRow/session-timezone behavior and the same bound per-column coercion/error
+ordering. Stage already-coerced integer/bool/float/date/timestamp/string values
+plus validity in at most 64-row blocks. No bulk append can flush a partial row;
+a terminal error discards staged buffers, including strings staged before a
+later-column coercion error. OFFSET/LIMIT still validate the required final-page
+tail and retain their existing output/error semantics.
+
+Flush staged columns at every 64-row staging boundary, actual public record
+boundary (including nonmultiples such as 65), and EOF. Public batch row counts,
+physical schema/NULL/default/exact-value behavior remain identical. String bulk
+append copies payloads into record-owned Arrow buffers; clear staging references
+after copy and release. Independently retained records survive Next/error/cancel/
+Release. Existing cursor cancellation, worker ownership and source pins remain.
+No public option, protocol/layout or publication change; this is not zero-copy.
+
+See [intent](intent.md), [plan](plan.md) and [validation](validation.md).
